      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "# Reading for Detail — The Life of Bees\n\nLittle bees are one of the most important insects on Earth. Honey bees live together in large groups called colonies, and one colony can have thousands of bees.\n\nIn each nest, every bee has its own job. Each nest has just one queen, and the queen's job is to lay eggs. The worker bees are all female. They clean the nest, care for the young bees and go out to find food.\n\nBees are famous for making honey. They collect a sweet liquid in flowers called nectar and turn it into honey, which they store for food.\n\nBees also help people and plants in another way. When they move from flower to flower, they carry pollen. This helps the plants make new seeds and fruit. When a bee finds many flowers, it flies back to the nest and does a special dance to show the other bees where the flowers are.\n\n---\n\n*Practice tip: When you read for detail, find the exact words in the text that answer the question. Check that the facts really match.*",
