      "passage_id": "2e882d2b-aedc-52f6-9c41-1ccfbfc30e78",
      "slug": "skimming-the-history-of-money",
      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "**A**  Long ago, there was no money at all. People got what they needed by swapping\nthings. A farmer with too much grain might give some to a fisherman for fish. This way\nof trading is called barter. It worked, but it was not easy.\n\n**B**  To make trading simpler, people began to use coins. The first metal coins were\nmade in a land called Lydia about 600 BC. The coins were small and made of metal, so\nthey were easy to carry and count.\n\n**C**  Coins had one big problem: they were heavy and hard to carry. People in China\nfound an answer. They began to use paper money, which was light and easy to fold. Over\ntime, it spread to other parts of the world.\n\n**D**  Today many people pay without coins or paper at all. They use plastic cards or a\nphone. This is money you cannot hold in your hand, and it may keep changing.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "Trong bài lịch sử, gạch chân các mốc năm + động từ quá khứ để định vị nhanh sự kiện khi làm matching headings hoặc detail.",
            "point": "Thì quá khứ đơn kể sự kiện đã qua (động từ bất quy tắc)",
            "review": "Quá khứ đơn: S + V-ed (hoặc động từ bất quy tắc: make→made, get→got, begin→began, find→found). Dùng cho sự việc đã xảy ra và kết thúc trong quá khứ.",
            "example": "The first metal coins **were made** in a land called Lydia … about 600 BC.",
            "analysis": "'were made' là quá khứ đơn dạng bị động ('were' là quá khứ của 'be' số nhiều + V3 'made'). Cả đoạn dùng quá khứ đơn (got, began, found) để kể chuỗi sự kiện lịch sử đã hoàn tất, gắn với mốc thời gian cụ thể 'about 600 BC'."
