      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "**A**  The spoon is one of the oldest tools in the world. Long before knives and forks, early\npeople needed a way to eat soup and other soft food. At first, they used simple things from\nnature. A large shell or a small piece of wood made a good early spoon.\n\n**B**  Later, people began to make spoons on purpose. In ancient Egypt, spoons were made\nfrom wood, stone, and even animal bone. Some special spoons were beautiful and were only\nused in temples. The rich liked spoons that showed their wealth.\n\n**C**  In ancient Rome, spoons changed again. Roman families used spoons made from bronze\nand silver. A poor family had a simple spoon, but a rich family ate with shiny silver. For\nhundreds of years, a spoon was a sign of money.\n\n**D**  Today, things are very different. Most spoons are made from cheap, strong metal, so\nalmost everyone in the world owns one.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
