    {
      "passage_id": "0c157b4b-a744-5f31-9ee4-b43ff152f4a0",
      "slug": "tfng-ynng-is-space-tourism-worth-it",
      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "For decades, space travel was the preserve of a handful of trained astronauts chosen by\ngovernments. That began to change in 2021, when private citizens who had bought tickets\ncrossed the boundary of space on craft built by private companies. A young space-tourism\nindustry was born, and with it a stubborn question: whether firing the rich into the sky\nfor a few minutes is really worth it.\n\nThe cost, in every sense, is high. A seat on a brief suborbital flight — one that merely\ntouches the edge of space and falls back — can run to hundreds of thousands of dollars,\nand longer trips into orbit cost far more. At such prices, critics argue, the money could\nbe better spent on more pressing problems at home.\n\nThere are serious risks to weigh, too. Rockets are dangerous machines, and even with\ncareful checks an accident remains possible. There are environmental worries as well:\nrockets release gases and soot high in the atmosphere, where their effects are still\npoorly understood. For some, polluting the sky so that a few people can enjoy the view is\nhard to justify.\n\nSupporters, however, point to benefits that may reach beyond the travellers themselves.\nThe race for customers has driven the development of reusable rockets, which may lower\nthe cost of other missions, including scientific research. The flights also carry\nexperiments and help test technology that could later serve more distant journeys. For\nthese people, today's tourists are quietly paying for tomorrow's progress.\n\nSo is space tourism worth it? The answer probably depends on how one weighs a rare, if\nfrivolous, experience against its price and its risks. Whether the industry matures into\nsomething more broadly useful, or remains an expensive game for the few, is too early to\nsay.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "Câu hỏi mở 'whether… is really worth it' báo hiệu tác giả CHƯA kết luận — gắn trực tiếp với đáp án NO (không tin chắc đáng giá) và NOT GIVEN cho quan điểm chưa nêu.",
            "point": "Mệnh đề danh ngữ với 'whether' làm tân ngữ và rào đón 'really'",
            "review": "whether + S + V = liệu… hay không; có thể làm chủ ngữ, tân ngữ hay bổ ngữ. V-ing làm chủ ngữ của mệnh đề (firing… is…).",
            "example": "a stubborn question: **whether firing the rich into the sky for a few minutes is really worth it**",
            "analysis": "'whether firing the rich into the sky … is really worth it' là mệnh đề danh ngữ làm phần giải thích cho 'question'. Chủ ngữ của mệnh đề là cụm danh động từ 'firing the rich into the sky'; 'worth it' = đáng giá. 'really' nhấn mạnh sự nghi vấn."
