      "library": "l1_vocab",
      "source_body_markdown": "On some cold, dark nights, the **sky** in the far north does something amazing.\nSoft lights of green, pink, and purple **glow** and move above the snow. People call\nthis beautiful show the Northern Lights.\n\nWhere do the lights come from? The story begins at **the Sun**. The Sun **sends out**\ntiny pieces all the time. These pieces **travel** a very long way through space to the\nEarth. When they reach us, they hit **gas** high in the sky. The gas then begins to\nglow, just like the lights in a sign. The most common colour is green.\n\nYou cannot see this show everywhere. The best places are in the far **north**, near\nthe top of the world, where the nights are very long in winter. You also need a dark,\n**clear** night with no clouds.\n\nIf you are ever in the right place at the right time, you are very **lucky**. The\nNorthern Lights are one of the most beautiful sights in nature.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
